:"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-9v[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Harden the bead subsystem against the verified gaps from the [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]post-sase-9r/9s review[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The verified bugs and inconsistencies from the five-reviewer [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]bead-subsystem audit are fixed: every runner bead mutation runs [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]under the store write lock, retained claims are always committed [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and publishable, claim residue is reconciled and visible to doctor,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]git probe failures fail closed, the managed sync worker clears [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]cooldowns and stops leaking process state, the bead_store_refresh [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]chop fits its own time budget, the `sase bead work` CLI honors its [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]confirmation/JSON/reporting contracts, legacy epic approvals stop [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]blocking the ACE event loop, sase-core bead mutations are atomic [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]against each other, dead code left by the recent refactors is [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]removed, and docs/beads.md matches current behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase/repos/plans/202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]bead_review_hardening.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Serialize the launch-claim mutation under the store write lock[bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]launch_claim_lock[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch_claim_lock: hold one bead_store_write_lock span across the runner[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch-claim mutation and its SDD commit in claim_bead_for_agent_launch,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]matching the sase-9r.1 contract already enforced on the wait-claim and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release paths.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Always commit retained claims and make release outcomes [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]tri-state[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]claim_persistence[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]claim_persistence: commit and publish a wait claim that is held but [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]still uncommitted after a retry, return distinct released/no-op/error [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]outcomes from claim release so shutdown can clear markers on no-ops, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]guard home-mode and in-tree claim publication, and enforce the push [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path's never-raises contract.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile claim residue and surface stuck beads in doctor[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]residue_diagnostics[dim] · [dim][/dim]after claim_persistence[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]residue_diagnostics: give the bead_claim_checks chop a terminal [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tombstone for dead-owner records so it regains its zero-read steady [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state, and add report-only doctor advisories for dead-owner [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]claimed/in_progress beads and dangling dependency edges.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Git probe failures must never read as clean[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]probe_fail_closed[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]probe_fail_closed: make bead_state_is_clean fail closed on probe errors,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]treat unexpected `git diff --cached` exit codes as errors in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit_sdd_files, and include unmerged_error in repository blockers and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollback-mismatch verification, finishing the sase-9r.3 sweep.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Managed sync worker cooldown, environment, redaction, and log [bold black on #87D7FF][/bold #D7AFFF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]fixes[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]sync_worker_hygiene[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync_worker_hygiene: clear the failed-integration cooldown marker on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every successful integration path, stop mutating os.environ in-process, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]redact credentials in sync worker git errors via the shared formatter, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]give detached sync logs a unique collision-free writer, and drop the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]worker's redundant freshness marking.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fit the bead_store_refresh chop inside its own time budget[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]refresh_chop_budget[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]refresh_chop_budget: bound the per-project lock wait of the chop's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]blocking refresh below the chop timeout, and persist backoff state so a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]timeout kill does not erase it; scoped to compose with the separately [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]planned sase-9u refresh_cooldown phase.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Restore the bead work CLI confirmation, JSON, and reporting [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]contracts[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]bead_work_cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead_work_cli: honor --yes/--yes-to-all on epic resume instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hardcoding force-approval, restore the epic-launch task origin, emit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]JSON envelopes on every bead-id error path, report only real phases as [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]phase beads, diagnose plan-file-only flags on bead-id targets, correct [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]misleading error/hint texts, and serialize bead-id launches under the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic launch lock.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Move legacy epic-approval preflight off the ACE event loop[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tui_epic_approval_offload[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui_epic_approval_offload: run the legacy plan-approval modal's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic-launch preflight and submission through the tracked-task pattern [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the modern gate path already uses, so store materialization and lock [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]waits never block the Textual event loop.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make every sase-core bead mutation atomic against concurrent [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]writers[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_mutation_atomicity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_mutation_atomicity: extend with_bead_mutation_lock to all bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]store mutations (not just the three claim functions), write JSONL [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through per-process temp files, align missing-dependency semantics [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]between ready/blocked reads and the epic work planner, and remove the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dead OperationOutcomeWire type. Implemented in the sase-core repo.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove dead code and duplicated helpers left by the recent [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]bead refactors[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]dead_code_cleanup[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]dead_code_cleanup: delete the orphaned imports, aliases, unreachable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]branches, duplicate exception arms, and dead parameters identified by [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the review, deduplicate the sync worker's git runner, and label the last[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unnamed store-lock call sites.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Align docs/beads.md and CLI help with current behavior[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs_truth[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs_truth: rewrite the stale claim-publication and Plan Approval Flow [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sections of docs/beads.md, add the missing sase bead work flags to its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flag table, and document that --json implies skipped confirmations in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the parser help.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-9v","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-9v.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-93064f009c7029dd8a7108e0829eeb7b","started_at":"2026-07-26T15:33:40.568454+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785085710,"sha":"896e024004e1ce40a5247f7c17583a092d24b8d2","subject":"fix(bead): reconcile claim residue and flag stuck beads (sase-9v.3)"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"315ea9a80eab807699e752641991fc663265345a6233d32570ff357dcb5b7d2f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-9v.3/chat.md","size_bytes":4883},"commits":{"digest":"d9ed3acbdbefefbc0b0adccb12